{"slug":"lab-value-remover-function","kind":"lab","title":"Value Remover Function","fetchedAt":"2026-10-16T02:56:10.461Z","items":[{"kind":"challenge","id":"a39963a4c10bc8b4d4f06d7e","title":"Implement a Value Remover Function","challengeType":26,"demoType":null,"description":"In this lab, you will create a function that takes an initial array as its first argument, followed by one or more additional arguments representing the values to remove.\n\n**Objective**: Fulfill the user stories below and get all the tests to pass to complete the lab.\n\n**User Stories:**\n\n1. You should have a `destroyer` function that accepts an array and one or more additional arguments.\n1. The `destroyer` function should return a new array excluding all elements from the first argument that match any of the subsequent arguments.\n1. The function must accept an indeterminate number of arguments.","hints":[{"text":"You should have a `destroyer` function.","test":"assert.isFunction(destroyer);"},{"text":"`destroyer([1, 2, 3, 1, 2, 3], 2, 3)` should return `[1, 1]`.","test":"assert.deepEqual(destroyer([1, 2, 3, 1, 2, 3], 2, 3), [1, 1]);"},{"text":"`destroyer([1, 2, 3, 5, 1, 2, 3], 2, 3)` should return `[1, 5, 1]`.","test":"assert.deepEqual(destroyer([1, 2, 3, 5, 1, 2, 3], 2, 3), [1, 5, 1]);"},{"text":"`destroyer([3, 5, 1, 2, 2], 2, 3, 5)` should return `[1]`.","test":"assert.deepEqual(destroyer([3, 5, 1, 2, 2], 2, 3, 5), [1]);"},{"text":"`destroyer([2, 3, 2, 3], 2, 3)` should return `[]`.","test":"assert.deepEqual(destroyer([2, 3, 2, 3], 2, 3), []);"},{"text":"`destroyer([\"tree\", \"hamburger\", 53], \"tree\", 53)` should return `[\"hamburger\"]`.","test":"assert.deepEqual(destroyer([\"tree\", \"hamburger\", 53], \"tree\", 53), [\"hamburger\"]);"},{"text":"`destroyer( [\"possum\", \"trollo\", 12, \"safari\", \"hotdog\", 92, 65, \"grandma\", \"bugati\", \"trojan\", \"yacht\"], \"yacht\", \"possum\", \"trollo\", \"safari\", \"hotdog\", \"grandma\", \"bugati\", \"trojan\" )` should return `[12, 92, 65]`.","test":"assert.deepEqual(\n  destroyer(\n    [\"possum\", \"trollo\", 12, \"safari\", \"hotdog\", 92, 65, \"grandma\", \"bugati\", \"trojan\", \"yacht\"],\n    \"yacht\", \"possum\", \"trollo\", \"safari\", \"hotdog\", \"grandma\", \"bugati\", \"trojan\"\n  ),\n  [12, 92, 65]\n);"}],"seed":"","seedLang":"js","region":null,"solution":"function destroyer(arr, ...valsToRemove) {\n  return arr.filter(item => !valsToRemove.includes(item));\n}","solutionLang":"js","beforeAll":"","beforeEach":""}]}